# Canonical image and tool version pins.
# All Dockerfiles and build scripts consume these via ARG / --build-arg.
# Update here only; the CI check-docker guard enforces consistency.
# Replace with your organisation's registry mirror prefix if applicable.
GO_IMAGE=golang:1.27-alpine@sha256:8a5910f31396cd4d89662f56c68b3ae31d374308270a1c3bd96672ee5ed43414
NODE_IMAGE=node:26-slim@sha256:ec7758ee051e457b468b32bde57b0879010b325bb9862718e9615225ce4aaae1
ALLOY_IMAGE=grafana/alloy:v1.20.1@sha256:2aa2099af76c0098d4af7a4d6e48f86cb66dc1a000222ad927a1c67c6542d13f
ALLOY_VERSION=v1.20.1
# The simulator image must RUN the Alloy binary, not just ship it. Alloy v1.18.1
# is dynamically linked (libc, libpthread, libdl, ld-linux), so distroless/static
# cannot exec it — the process dies with "no such file or directory", which is the
# loader, not the binary. distroless/base carries glibc and nothing else.
# base-nossl, not base: every image here holds a static Go binary (CGO_ENABLED=0,
# zero DT_NEEDED entries) plus grafana/alloy, and alloy links only glibc —
# libpthread, libdl, libc, ld-linux, verified with readelf. Neither needs
# OpenSSL, so shipping it would be CVE surface nothing links against.
#
# NOT distroless/static: alloy is dynamically linked, and static carries no
# dynamic loader — the binary lands in the image unrunnable and Stage 2 of the
# validation gate silently dies. `make check-alloy-runnable` guards that.
DISTROLESS_BASE_IMAGE=gcr.io/distroless/base-nossl-debian12:nonroot@sha256:be40c00dfabd86576d92666e87e406714d5618342de1a0c213ad232de255172e
PNPM_VERSION=12.8.1
# Every image is pinned by DIGEST as well as tag: the tag says what it is, the
# digest says exactly which build, so a base image republished under the same
# tag cannot change what the release ships without a reviewed PR. Renovate
# (renovate.json) refreshes digests and proposes tag bumps; Dependabot cannot
# read these lines. ALLOY_IMAGE tag bumps are a schema bump and stay manual.
# Scanners run by `make secrets-scan` / `make image-scan` / `make config-scan`
# and by .github/workflows/security-scan.yml — pinned by digest so CI and a
# laptop scan with the same rule set.
GITLEAKS_IMAGE=ghcr.io/gitleaks/gitleaks:v8.30.0@sha256:105ac66a57b2bb8afb61a3b8a5dcc4817773d03724a7e8a515214cfe58225556
TRIVY_IMAGE=aquasec/trivy:0.74.0@sha256:ee940acbf1f58ebadb42d01434ce4609530bf1b52536afbd1eee66cd7123c5c9

# Gateway API (docs/gateway-tier-plan.md D1/D2). This is BOTH the minimum
# Shepherd accepts at runtime and the version the kind suite installs — we test
# against the floor we claim, because that is what proves the claim.
#
# The 1.4 line is the baseline because it is what most controllers ship today.
# Channel is Standard, and that matters more than the number: verified against
# v1.4.0's own CRDs on 2026-08-21, the Standard channel contains URLRewrite and
# ReplacePrefixMatch (both used) but NOT the CORS filter — CORS only appears in
# the Experimental channel at 1.4, and reaches Standard in v1.6.1. That is why
# Alloy's faro.receiver answers CORS instead of the gateway (D2); revisit only
# if the floor ever rises past 1.6.
GATEWAY_API_VERSION=v1.4.1
GATEWAY_API_CHANNEL=standard

# Grafana k8s-monitoring chart (docs/gateway-tier-plan.md W9, G8). Pins the
# exact release internal/chartvalues.PinnedChartVersion targets and the
# release testdata/values.schema.json and testdata/values.schema.meta.json
# were vendored from. Unlike GATEWAY_API_VERSION this is a MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH
# pin, not a floor: a Helm chart's values shape is not a versioned API with a
# deprecation window, so "newer accepts the same input" cannot be assumed —
# see internal/chartvalues/version.go.
#
# Bump procedure: update this value, re-fetch values.schema.json from
# https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/k8s-monitoring-helm/k8s-monitoring-<version>/charts/k8s-monitoring/values.schema.json,
# update values.schema.meta.json's chart_version/source_url/release_tag/
# fetched_at/sha256 together, update PinnedChartVersion to match, then run
# `make check-chartvalues-pin` and `make chart-verify`.
K8S_MONITORING_CHART_VERSION=4.4.0

# Optional chart dependencies, exercised by the kind suite (e2e/k8s/
# chart_deps_test.go). Neither operator is installed by Shepherd's chart and
# neither is required to run it — these pins exist so the suite proves the
# integrations against real controllers rather than against `helm template`.
#
# Pinned exactly, not as a floor: both charts render CRDs, and "a newer
# version accepts the same input" is not a promise either project makes.
#
# The External Secrets pin must stay on a chart that serves
# external-secrets.io/v1. Verified against 2.9.0's own CRDs on 2026-08-25, and
# re-verified against 2.11.0's (deploy/crds/bundle.yaml at v2.11.0) on
# 2026-10-01: externalsecrets/secretstores/clustersecretstores serve v1 and not
# v1beta1, and passwords.generators.external-secrets.io still serves v1alpha1 —
# the two apiVersions deploy/helm/shepherd/values.yaml defaults to.
# CNPG 0.29.1 is operator 1.30.1 (a patch over 0.29.0's 1.30.0), kubeVersion
# floor unchanged at >= 1.29.0-0.
CNPG_CHART_VERSION=0.29.1
EXTERNAL_SECRETS_CHART_VERSION=2.11.0

# kind node image for BOTH the e2e suite (e2e/k8s/main_test.go, E2E_K8S_NODE_IMAGE still
# wins) and the dev stack (scripts/dev-kind.sh). Tag only, no digest, and EXCLUDED from
# Renovate (renovate.json): a bump must stay inside kind v0.33 / helm/kind-action support,
# above NGF 2.7.2's kubeVersion floor (>= 1.32.0-0) and CNPG 0.29.1's (>= 1.29.0-0) —
# a reviewed decision, not a Monday PR. v1.37.0 is kind v0.33.0's default node image
# (its release notes list v1.37.0 / v1.36.4 / v1.35.8 / v1.34.11 as built for it), and
# helm/kind-action v1.15.0 installs kind v0.33.0. The chart's kubeVersion floor is
# >= 1.32 (chart 0.19.0): the lowest version this suite's NGF supports.
KIND_NODE_IMAGE=kindest/node:v1.37.0
# Calico manifest tag applied after cluster creation (disableDefaultCNI). A CNI upgrade
# changing enforcement must be a deliberate commit — see e2e/k8s/main_test.go installCNI.
# v3.32 removed AdminNetworkPolicy/BaselineAdminNetworkPolicy enforcement (replaced by
# ClusterNetworkPolicy); this repo uses only networking.k8s.io/v1 NetworkPolicy.
CALICO_VERSION=v3.32.2
# NGINX Gateway Fabric chart, the Gateway API controller the suite proves conformance
# against and the dev stack routes through — see route_conformance_test.go for why NGF.
# 2.7.x is built against Gateway API 1.6.1 while GATEWAY_API_VERSION stays at the 1.4.1
# floor; NGF discovers which CRDs are installed (since 2.4.0) rather than requiring its
# own bundle version, and the kind suite is what proves that combination.
NGF_CHART_VERSION=2.7.2
